        <h2>1. Executive Summary</h2>
        <p>
            Project Aegis aims to revolutionize the daily lived experience of individuals with physical and sensory disabilities. 
            Current assistive technologies often exist in silos, failing to communicate with one another. Our research proposes 
            a unified, AI-driven framework that synchronizes smart-home environments, wearable haptics, and urban navigation 
            systems to create a seamless "safety net" for users.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Research Objectives</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Interoperability:</strong> Developing a universal protocol for assistive devices to communicate in real-time.</li>
            <li><strong>Predictive Assistance:</strong> Utilizing machine learning to anticipate user needs (e.g., adjusting lighting or mobility aids before a struggle occurs).</li>
            <li><strong>Urban Accessibility:</strong> Mapping "invisible barriers" in city infrastructure using crowdsourced data.</li>
        </ul>

